to Xfinity Mobile.

00:00:12.215 --> 00:00:13.745
And the number that wins the deal?

00:00:13.835 --> 00:00:15.225
The yearly savings.

00:00:15.495 --> 00:00:16.425
Let's go!

00:00:16.875 --> 00:00:17.965
Step 1.

00:00:18.255 --> 00:00:20.365
Start with the Xfinity membership tier.

00:00:20.495 --> 00:00:24.205
Some device promotions are tier
specific, so lock it in first.

00:00:24.555 --> 00:00:26.125
Today's customer is Silver.

00:00:27.188 --> 00:00:28.258
Step 2.

00:00:28.527 --> 00:00:29.427
Core savings.

00:00:29.628 --> 00:00:31.388
Pull up the customer's
core bill and find

00:00:31.428 --> 00:00:34.458
what they save by re-bundling
with Xfinity Mobile.

00:00:34.748 --> 00:00:35.837
Gig-speed internet.

00:00:36.028 --> 00:00:37.378
$135 today.

00:00:37.608 --> 00:00:39.218
Re-bundled. $95.

00:00:39.568 --> 00:00:41.557
Boom! $40 a month.

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:43.658
$480 a year.

00:00:43.727 --> 00:00:46.518
And it's sitting in green
at the top of the sheet.

00:00:46.875 --> 00:00:49.605
That running tally is the big picture!

00:00:49.875 --> 00:00:53.565
Core savings and mobile savings
combined into one number.

00:00:53.675 --> 00:00:56.925
We're hunting family ports,
so every dollar matters.

00:00:57.188 --> 00:00:59.778
Step 3. The mobile discount.

00:01:00.047 --> 00:01:03.128
Tell the customer, there's
a discount you qualify for.

00:01:03.168 --> 00:01:04.597
It's our mobile discount.

00:01:04.888 --> 00:01:06.617
Who do you have your cell phones with?

00:01:06.727 --> 00:01:08.438
Pick the carrier, Verizon.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:09.718
How many lines?

00:01:09.948 --> 00:01:10.587
Four.

00:01:10.627 --> 00:01:12.817
And what does that bill
cost you every month?

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:13.987
$300.

00:01:14.028 --> 00:01:15.037
Type it in.

00:01:15.938 --> 00:01:17.387
Now look up top!

00:01:17.718 --> 00:01:19.867
$190 a month!

00:01:21.157 --> 00:01:22.987
$2,280 a year!

00:01:23.438 --> 00:01:26.567
Here's the key to winning,
apples to apples.

00:01:26.698 --> 00:01:28.817
Four lines, quote four lines.

00:01:28.858 --> 00:01:31.227
Three lines, three watches,
three tablets,

00:01:31.338 --> 00:01:34.227
quote exactly that, don't get fancy.

00:01:34.358 --> 00:01:37.117
Add things they don't have
and customers say no.

00:01:37.157 --> 00:01:40.617
Not because it's a bad deal,
because they don't understand it.

00:01:40.657 --> 00:01:44.037
Keep it clean, show the side
by side and let them decide.

00:01:44.078 --> 00:01:47.907
The whole point of the T-chart is to
show the value of making the switch.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.440
Step 4. Keep them on Mobile Plus.

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:54.560
It has the most benefits
and the best service.

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:56.920
And skip the device financing for now.

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:59.620
Bring your own device keeps
their out-of-pocket low.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.160
No money down today.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:02.980
BYOD when you can.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:04.720
Now hit Build Comparison.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:06.715
Step 5.

00:02:06.985 --> 00:02:08.795
Present it, side by side.

00:02:08.945 --> 00:02:12.285
Your four lines at Verizon
cost you $300 a month.

00:02:12.325 --> 00:02:15.015
Switch them to Xfinity and you pay $150.

00:02:15.185 --> 00:02:18.595
With your home savings,
that's $190 a month.

00:02:18.685 --> 00:02:21.715
$2,280 this year.

00:02:21.965 --> 00:02:25.255
Then pause and ask, what do you think?

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.120
If they say yes,
go sell them some phones.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:32.100
If they say no, always ask why.

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:37.180
What's stopping you from putting
$2,280 back in your pocket this year?

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.340
Always lean on the biggest number.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.520
It's easy to walk away from $190.

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:44.700
It's very hard to walk away from $2,280.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.490
Then use the rest of the chart
to overcome the objection.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.050
Show them the home savings.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.230
Show them what comes with Mobile Plus.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.250
Truly unlimited data.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.270
XMC.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:59.070
International calls and texts
in over 250 destinations.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.490
Still a no? You have two moves.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:03.460
Move one.

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:05.270
Lower the bill with Mobile Select.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.190
Maybe they don't need XMC.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:09.360
Maybe they don't upgrade
every few months.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:14.130
Now it's $90 a month and
$3,000 in savings this year.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.090
Move two.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.920
If they flat out refuse
to switch their phones,

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.770
click Customer Declines Mobile
Offer at the bottom of the page.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:25.340
The sheet flips to devices-only mode.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:27.710
And this is where the
core savings matter.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:31.330
You can still save the money
without moving a single line.

00:03:31.875 --> 00:03:36.315
Add a tablet, add a watch, or move
their home phone to Xfinity Mobile.

00:03:36.355 --> 00:03:39.005
Pick the right product
and hit Build Comparison.

00:03:39.335 --> 00:03:40.315
Look at this one!

00:03:40.355 --> 00:03:43.055
Their bill drops $3 a
month and they walk out

00:03:43.095 --> 00:03:46.385
with an iPad with data they
can use anywhere they travel.

00:03:46.515 --> 00:03:49.665
The more you save on the core bill,
the better this offer gets.

00:03:50.625 --> 00:03:51.995
So here's the play.

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:55.015
Find what's right for the
customer and for you.

00:03:55.185 --> 00:03:57.795
Always ask, what's in
it for my customer?

00:03:57.985 --> 00:03:59.155
What's in it for me?

00:03:59.345 --> 00:04:03.775
Offer win-win solutions and you will
find tremendous success in sales.

00:04:03.945 --> 00:04:08.255
Be a problem solver with Xfinity
Mobile and the 6th Gen Quote Sheet.

00:04:08.305 --> 00:04:09.655
Now let's go cook!

